1	# @flexpa/mcp-fhir
2	
3	> [!WARNING]
4	> This is an experimental demo not intended for production use.
5	
6	This is a TypeScript-based MCP server that connects to a FHIR server. It provides core MCP functionality for interacting with FHIR resources by:
7	
8	- Accessing FHIR resources via URIs
9	- Providing search capabilities for FHIR resources
10	
11	## Features
12	
13	### Resources
14	
15	> [!TIP]
16	> "Resources" here refers to the MCP definition _not_ the FHIR one. MCP Resources are a core primitive in the Model Context Protocol (MCP) that allow servers to expose data and content that can be read by clients and used as context for LLM interactions.
17	
18	- List and access FHIR resources via `fhir://` URIs
19	- Resources are returned in FHIR JSON format
20	- Supports all FHIR Resource types available in the FHIR server's CapabilityStatement
21	
22	### Tools
23	- `search_fhir` - Search FHIR resources
24	  - Takes `resourceType` and `searchParams` as parameters
25	  - Returns FHIR search results
26	- `read_fhir` - Read an individual FHIR resource
27	  - Takes `uri` as a parameter
28	  - Returns the FHIR resource in JSON format
29	
30	## Configuration
31	
32	The server requires the following environment variables:
33	- `FHIR_BASE_URL`: The base URL of your FHIR server
34	- `FHIR_ACCESS_TOKEN`: A SMART on FHIR access token for authentication
35	
36	## Development
37	
38	Install dependencies:
39	```bash
40	npm install
41	```
42	
43	Build the server:
44	```bash
45	npm run build
46	```
47	
48	For development with auto-rebuild:
49	```bash
50	npm run watch
51	```
52	
53	## Installation
54	
55	To use with Claude Desktop, add the server config:
56	
57	On MacOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
58	On Windows: `%APPDATA%/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
59	
60	```json
61	{
62	  "mcpServers": {
63	    "fhir": {
64	      "command": "/path/to/@flexpa/mcp-fhir/build/index.js"
65	    },
66	    "env": {
67	      "FHIR_BASE_URL": "<FHIR_BASE_URL>",
68	      "FHIR_ACCESS_TOKEN": "<FHIR_ACCESS_TOKEN>"
69	    }
70	  }
71	}
72	```
73	
74	### Debugging
75	
76	Since MCP servers communicate over stdio, debugging can be challenging. We recommend using the [MCP Inspector](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector), which is available as a package script:
77	
78	```bash
79	npm run inspector
80	```
81	
82	The Inspector will provide a URL to access debugging tools in your browser.
83	

